/vet, ordinary full suite, proportionate race, and pinned lint, attach cycle-2 implementation/gate evidence, then developer handoff. Hardened containment remains separate/non-gating STORY-260728-327soo.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-eb5a56, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-eb5a56)\nRework cycle 2 in progress 2026-07-28. R3 root cause confirmed at its source: curator hybrid add|rm call scopes.AddHybridDecl/RemoveHybridDecl straight from cmd/curator/main.go:985,994 under no project, key, or home lock, so the machine-home hybrid activation manifest projectAttempt reads at step 5 could move at any point before the commit. Fix: the observation set and its path map now start at step 5 instead of step 16, and scopes.HybridManifestPath(cfg.Home()) is observed under key activation/hybrid-manifest. Ordering is digest-then-read on purpose - a writer racing the read leaves a recorded digest that no longer matches the file so the recheck restarts, whereas read-then-digest would record the writer bytes while the closure came from the bytes we read and commit stale activation. recheck already maps a generation difference to restartClosure and runCommit already calls it after recovery and before both cache publication and target staging, so no control flow changed. Closure-input audit completed and recorded in the observations doc comment; the user configuration is documented as a boundary, not claimed safe. 4 new tests in internal/install/atomicity/activation_test.go: a stable-manifest control that must NOT restart, plus removed, retargeted, and newly-applicable declarations. Negative control run: with the single observe line removed all three mutation cases fail and the control still passes. The reviewer overlay repro passes unmodified against the fix.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-eb5a56, pid=37927, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 COMPLETION DIRECTIVE 2026-07-28: continue in the same uncommitted worktree /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree. The R3 code, activation_test.go regressions, negative control, unchanged reviewer overlay pass, format/build/vet, and ordinary go test ./... are already present/green; preserve them and do not redo broad implementation or full suite. The prior run exited early because its broad race shell was killed externally and gate-test-race.log is empty, so it is not evidence. Run bounded incremental race checks for the changed hybrid-observation/restart path and its new activation tests, split into commands that complete under the harness or use a durable exit-file protocol. Capture exact exits. Run pinned repo-wide lint once, package a cycle-2 implementation note and gate archive, record the activation-input audit and any remaining boundary honestly, then developer handoff to to-review. Do not claim the empty broad race log and do not alter hardened STORY-260728-327soo.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-08f610, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-08f610)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 COMPLETE, ready for review. R3 closed at its source in .temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree (base origin/main 17804ce; nothing staged or committed). The machine-home hybrid activation manifest is now an optimistic observation: the observation set and its path map start at step 5 instead of step 16 and scopes.HybridManifestPath(cfg.Home()) is observed under key activation/hybrid-manifest before the manifest is read. Ordering is digest-then-read on purpose - a writer racing the read leaves a recorded digest that no longer matches the file so the recheck restarts, whereas read-then-digest would record the writer bytes while the closure came from the bytes actually read and commit stale activation; a bounded spurious restart is always the safe direction. No control flow changed: recheck already maps a generation difference to restartClosure and runCommit already calls it after journal recovery and before both cache publication and target staging (verified ordering at commit.go:402-445 - home lock, Recover, recheck, stage root, publishWinners, stageTargets, consumer last). Closure-input audit recorded in the observations doc comment and independently re-verified this cycle: LoadHybridDecls/HybridManifestPath have exactly one install-path caller (install.go:237,239); the other two (cmd/curator/main.go:1000,1010) are read-only hybrid list/status; global.go reads no hybrid manifest and locks GlobalRoot(home) at line 46 before any manifest read. The user-configuration row is documented as a BOUNDARY, not a freshness proof - per-attempt reloading is a separate decision. TESTS: 4 new cases in internal/install/atomicity/activation_test.go - a stable-manifest control that must NOT restart, plus removed, retargeted (declaration still exists, only targets moved, so an is-it-still-declared check cannot pass it) and newly-applicable declarations; each asserts the restart named closure resolution and activation/hybrid-manifest, that no stale hybrid context and no stale adapter mirror committed via Lstat/Readlink, that the project declaration still installed, and that no journal survived. Negative control: with the single observe line removed all three mutation cases fail and the control still passes; restored and re-verif