The submitted one-way regressions are green, and the earlier transaction/symlink/activation fixes remain green. I found a separate acceptance blocker in the observation design: the digest is taken before the read, but the read bytes are never bound to that digest. A supported writer sequence A → B → A between those two points lets the install build closure B, revalidate A successfully, and commit B. The deterministic overlay reproduces exactly that stale commit.
